Z||000000||BBBAD GT||10-01-2000||05:39 PM||||Welp, I mocked up a plate out of black cardboard, and fit the 2 1/16" electric autometer gauges (sport comp) in the aux pod this weekend for the V8 Fiero.  They look alot better than I first thought, and I'm glad I went with the 2 1/16" instead of the 2 5/8", it would of been a little too crowded.  The second part will comprise of swapping in 3 3/8" autometer tach and speedo into where the stock ones were (same as Batboy).  What do you guys think?<P> <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/gauge.jpg"> <P>Never-mind my smerk....<P>BTW, if you are wondering why I didn't go with the stock gauges, its because there are already the same gauges mounted where the stock tach was cept 1.5" autogauge units, and they are very difficult to read.  Also, the wiring is already there, and the stock wiring isn't.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||6
